    "id": "lesson-U-2QA0",
    "moduleId": "strategies",
    "title": "Strategy 2: Breakout & Retest",
    "summary": "How to trade confirmed breakouts of key levels by waiting for the retest — a high-probability continuation entry used by professional gold traders.",
    "body": "# Strategy 2: Breakout & Retest\n\n> **The Edge:** Most retail traders chase the breakout candle and get trapped. Professionals wait for the retest — when the broken level flips its role and confirms the new direction.\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 The Core Idea\n\nA **breakout** happens when price moves decisively beyond a key support or resistance level. But the real opportunity isn't in the breakout itself — it's in the **retest** that follows.\n\nWhen a resistance level is broken to the upside, it often **becomes new support**. When a support level is broken to the downside, it often **becomes new resistance**. This \"role reversal\" is one of the most reliable phenomena in all of technical analysis — and it's especially powerful in gold.\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 Why Does the Retest Happen?\n\nThink about the participants involved:\n\n- **Breakout buyers** entered long when price broke the resistance\n- **Late buyers** missed the move and are waiting for a pullback to enter\n- **Stop-loss sellers** who were short below resistance have now been stopped out\n- The result: when price pulls back to the broken level, **buyers defend it aggressively** — causing the bounce\n\n---\n\n## 📐 Step-by-Step Process (Bullish Breakout)\n\n### Step 1 — Identify the Key Level\n- Look for a **clear, well-tested resistance level** on the 1H or 4H chart\n- The more times price has rejected it, the more significant the break will be\n- Example: Gold has rejected **$3,750** three times over two days\n\n### Step 2 — Wait for a Clean Breakout\nA valid breakout must be:\n- ✅ A **strong candle close** above the level (not just a wick)\n- ✅ Ideally on **above-average momentum** (large candle body)\n- ✅ During an **active session** (London or New York — not Asia)\n- ❌ NOT a slow, grinding grind through the level (weak breakout = high false breakout risk)\n\n### Step 3 — Wait for the Retest\n- After the breakout, price will often **pull back toward the broken level**\n- You are NOT entering on the breakout candle itself\n- You wait for price to return to the **$3,750 zone** (former resistance, now support)\n- This pullback may take 15 minutes or several hours — patience is required\n\n### Step 4 — Look for a Trigger at the Retest\nAt the retest zone, look for:\n- 🕯️ A **bullish rejection candle** (pin bar, hammer, bullish engulfing)\n- 📌 A **liquidity sweep** below the retest zone (stop hunt) followed by recovery\n- 🔺 A **5m or 15m break of structure** to the upside after touching the zone\n- 📊 Price spending minimal time at the level (quick bounce = strong defence)\n\n### Step 5 — Invalidation\n- If price **closes back below** the broken level ($3,750), the breakout has failed\n- This is your stop — place it just below the retest zone\n- A failed breakout (false breakout) is a separate setup — do not hold through it\n\n### Step 6 — Target\n- **Minimum:** 1.5–2× your stop distance (2R minimum)\n- **Primary:** The next resistance level above — measured moves work well here\n- **Extended:** If price broke out of a range, the target is often the **height of the range** added to the breakout point\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Bearish Breakout (Mirror Image)\n\n| Step | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Key Level | Clear support at $3,700, tested multiple times |\n| Breakout | Strong bearish close below $3,700 |\n| Retest | Price pulls back UP to $3,700 (now resistance) |\n| Trigger | Bearish engulfing / sweep of highs / 5m structure break down |\n| Stop | Above $3,700 zone |\n| Target | Next support level below — aim for 2R+ |\n\n---\n\n## 🔑 Qualities of a High-Probability Breakout & Retest\n\n| Factor | Low Quality | High Quality |\n|---|---|---|\n| Level tested | Once or twice | 3+ times |\n| Breakout candle | Small, slow close | Large, fast, strong close |\n| Session | Asian session | London or NY open |\n| Retest behaviour | Price lingers at level | Quick bounce off level |\n| HTF alignment | Counter-trend | In direction of 4H trend |\n| Confluence | None | Fib level, round number, or session level at same zone |\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| Entering on the breakout candle | Wait for the retest — always |\n| Taking every breakout regardless of quality | Only trade levels tested 3+ times with strong breakout candles |\n| Not accounting for spread at the level | Give the zone a few dollars of buffer |\n| Ignoring the HTF trend | Breakout retests in the trend direction have far higher success rates |\n| Setting target too close | Minimum 2R — otherwise the math doesn't work over time |\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Summary\n\n| Element | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Context** | 4H trend confirmed; key level clearly defined |\n| **Location** | Broken support (now resistance) or broken resistance (now support) |\n| **Scenario** | IF price breaks key level AND retests it AND shows rejection THEN continue in breakout direction |\n| **Trigger** | Rejection candle, liquidity sweep, or 5m structure break at retest zone |\n| **Invalidation** | Close back beyond the broken level |\n| **Target** | Next structure level — minimum 2R |",
