    "id": "lesson-H8IFJm",
    "moduleId": "strategies",
    "title": "Strategy 5: Support & Resistance Rejection",
    "summary": "How to trade confirmed rejections at strong support and resistance zones — one of the cleanest and most beginner-friendly setups in gold trading.",
    "body": "# Strategy 5: Support & Resistance Rejection\n\n> **The Edge:** Strong S/R zones have memory. Price has reversed at these levels before, and it often does again. A confirmed rejection candle at a tested zone is one of the clearest entries in gold trading.\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 The Core Idea\n\n**Support** is a price zone where buying pressure historically exceeded selling pressure — price fell into it and bounced up. **Resistance** is the opposite — price rose into it and was pushed back down.\n\nThe reason these levels \"work\" repeatedly is simple: **traders have memory**. Participants who bought at a support level before will buy there again. Those who sold at resistance will sell there again. This self-fulfilling behaviour creates zones that act as magnets and barriers simultaneously.\n\nA **rejection** at these zones is your entry signal — confirmation that the level is still \"alive.\"\n\n---\n\n## 📐 How to Identify Strong S/R Zones\n\nNot all levels are equal. A strong S/R zone has:\n\n| Quality | What to Look For |\n|---|---|\n| **Multiple touches** | Price has reacted at the same zone 2–4+ times |\n| **Clean reactions** | Each touch produced a sharp, decisive reversal |\n| **Higher timeframe origin** | The zone is visible and significant on the 4H or Daily chart |\n| **Round number alignment** | The zone sits near $3,700, $3,750, $3,800, etc. |\n| **Recent relevance** | The zone was tested within the last 5–20 trading days |\n\n> ✅ The best zones are those where you can see them **without squinting** — they are obvious to everyone.\n\n---\n\n## 📐 Step-by-Step Process (Support Rejection — Buy)\n\n### Step 1 — Identify a Strong Support Zone\n- Look at the **1H or 4H chart**\n- Find a zone where price has bounced **at least twice** before\n- Draw a **zone** (not a line) — from the lowest wick to the top of the candle bodies that reacted\n\n### Step 2 — Confirm 4H Bias is Bullish\n- The support rejection only has high probability if the **higher timeframe trend is bullish**\n- You are buying a dip in a bull trend — not trying to catch a falling knife\n\n### Step 3 — Wait for Price to Enter the Zone\n- Do NOT jump in as soon as price approaches the zone\n- Wait for price to **actually enter** the zone\n- Watch what happens next — is there immediate rejection or does price linger?\n\n### Step 4 — Look for a Rejection Candle (Trigger)\nValid rejection signals include:\n\n| Candle Type | Description |\n|---|---|\n| **Pin Bar / Hammer** | Long lower wick, small body — price was pushed down but recovered strongly |\n| **Bullish Engulfing** | Large bullish candle that completely engulfs the previous bearish candle |\n| **Tweezer Bottom** | Two candles with the same low — double rejection at the exact level |\n| **Inside Bar Reversal** | A tight consolidation inside the zone, followed by a bullish breakout candle |\n\n> ✅ The rejection candle must **close** — never enter on an unfinished candle\n\n### Step 5 — Entry\n- Enter at the **close of the rejection candle** (or the open of the next candle)\n- Use a **limit order** just inside the zone if you prefer a more precise entry\n\n### Step 6 — Invalidation\n- Stop goes just **below the lowest wick** of the support zone\n- If price closes below the zone, support has broken — do not hold\n\n### Step 7 — Target\n- **First target:** The most recent swing high above\n- **Second target:** The next significant resistance level\n- Minimum **2R** — if the target is less than 2R away, skip the trade\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Resistance Rejection (Sell) — Mirror Image\n\n| Step | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Find Zone | Clear resistance zone tested 2+ times on 1H/4H |\n| HTF Bias | 4H is bearish |\n| Wait | Price enters the resistance zone |\n| Trigger | Bearish pin bar, bearish engulfing, or tweezer top |\n| Entry | Close of rejection candle |\n| Stop | Just above the highest wick of the resistance zone |\n| Target | Next support level below — minimum 2R |\n\n---\n\n## 🔑 Confluence Factors That Strengthen the Setup\n\n| Confluence | Why It Helps |\n|---|---|\n| Fibonacci 0.618 at the same zone | Two independent tools pointing to the same level |\n| Round number ($3,750, $3,800) | Psychological magnet — more orders clustered here |\n| Session high/low aligns with zone | Adds institutional significance |\n| 4H or Daily trend aligns | Trading with the \"big money\" direction |\n| Volume spike on rejection candle | Confirms institutional participation at the level |\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| Buying support in a bearish 4H trend | Check HTF bias first — never buy into a strong downtrend |\n| Entering before the rejection candle closes | Wait for the close — an unfinished candle can still flip |\n| Treating old, distant zones as valid | Zones lose strength over time — focus on recent reactions |\n| Setting target too close (less than 2R) | If R/R is poor, skip the trade entirely |\n| Re-entering after a zone has clearly broken | A broken zone is no longer valid support/resistance |\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Summary\n\n| Element | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Context** | 4H trend bullish (for support play) or bearish (for resistance play) |\n| **Location** | Strong S/R zone tested 2–4+ times on 1H or 4H |\n| **Scenario** | IF price enters the zone AND produces a rejection candle THEN trade in the direction of the rejection |\n| **Trigger** | Pin bar, engulfing candle, or tweezer at the zone — confirmed close |\n| **Invalidation** | Candle closes beyond the far edge of the zone |\n| **Target** | Next structure level — minimum 2R |",
