    "moduleId": "strategies",
    "title": "Strategy 15: Order Block Entry",
    "summary": "How to identify and trade from Order Blocks — the footprints left by institutional buying and selling in gold.",
    "body": "# Strategy 15: Order Block Entry\n\n> **The Edge:** Order Blocks are zones where institutions placed large buy or sell orders. Price frequently returns to these zones — giving you a high-probability entry point with a tight, logical stop.\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 The Core Idea\n\nAn **Order Block (OB)** is the last opposing candle before a strong impulsive move. It represents an area where a large institution placed a significant order — causing the explosive move that followed.\n\nBecause institutions often have **unfilled orders** remaining at these levels, price tends to return to them to \"fill\" the remaining orders before continuing in the original direction.\n\nThink of it as: **institutions left their fingerprints on the chart — and you trade when price returns to those fingerprints.**\n\n---\n\n## 📐 How to Identify an Order Block\n\n### Bullish Order Block (Demand Zone)\n1. Look for a **strong bullish impulse** — several consecutive bullish candles moving sharply upward\n2. Find the **last bearish candle** BEFORE that impulse began\n3. That bearish candle's **body** = your bullish Order Block zone\n4. Mark the **high and low of that candle's body** as your zone\n\n### Bearish Order Block (Supply Zone)\n1. Look for a **strong bearish impulse** — several consecutive bearish candles moving sharply downward\n2. Find the **last bullish candle** BEFORE that impulse began\n3. That bullish candle's **body** = your bearish Order Block zone\n4. Mark the **high and low of that candle's body** as your zone\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Visual Example\n\n```\nBearish Order Block:\n         [Last bullish candle] ← This is the OB zone\n              ↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓\n         Strong bearish impulse\n\nPrice returns to the OB zone → SELL trigger\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📐 Step-by-Step Process (Bearish Order Block)\n\n### Step 1 — Confirm HTF Bias (4H)\n- Structure is bearish (LH, LL)\n- The most recent move was a strong bearish impulse\n\n### Step 2 — Identify the Order Block (1H)\n- Find the last bullish candle before the bearish impulse\n- Mark its body as your supply/OB zone\n- The zone should have caused a **clear, strong move away** — not a slow drift\n\n### Step 3 — Wait for Price to Return\n- Do NOT enter immediately — wait for price to retrace back UP into the OB zone\n- This retracement is the pullback phase\n\n### Step 4 — Look for a Trigger at the OB\n- Bearish rejection candle inside the OB zone (pin bar, engulfing, shooting star)\n- Liquidity sweep above the OB zone's high, then reversal back inside\n- 5m break of structure to the downside from within the zone\n\n### Step 5 — Invalidation\n- Stop goes **above the top of the Order Block zone**\n- If price closes convincingly above the OB, it is consumed/broken — exit immediately\n\n### Step 6 — Target\n- First target: Previous swing low (the low of the impulse that created the OB)\n- Second target: Next major structure low\n- Minimum 2R before entry\n\n---\n\n## 🔑 What Makes a Strong Order Block?\n\n| Characteristic | Why It Matters |\n|---|---|\n| **Strong move away from the zone** | Proves institutional involvement |\n| **Clean, untested zone** | First return to OB = strongest reaction |\n| **Aligns with HTF structure** | Confluence = higher probability |\n| **Near a key level** | Round numbers, session highs/lows add confluence |\n| **Clear imbalance (gap) after OB** | Shows urgency — institutions were aggressive |\n\n---\n\n## 🔑 Order Block vs Regular S/R\n\n| Feature | Order Block | Regular S/R |\n|---|---|---|\n| Origin | Last candle before impulse | Multiple touches over time |\n| Precision | Very specific candle body | Broader zone |\n| Strength | Strongest on first retest | Gets weaker with each touch |\n| Concept | Institutional footprint | Market memory |\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| Marking every candle as an OB | Only the last opposing candle before a STRONG impulse |\n| Trading OBs against the HTF trend | Always align with 4H bias |\n| Entering without a trigger | Wait for rejection inside the zone — don't anticipate |\n| Ignoring consumed OBs | If price has already closed through the OB, it's invalid |\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Pre-Trade Checklist\n\n- [ ] 4H structure confirms the directional bias\n- [ ] A clear strong impulse move exists with an identifiable OB\n- [ ] The OB zone is clean (not yet retested)\n- [ ] Price has returned to the OB zone\n- [ ] A trigger candle has formed inside the zone\n- [ ] Stop is placed beyond the far edge of the OB\n- [ ] Target gives minimum 2R\n- [ ] No major news event imminent",
