    "id": "lesson-UsXDjJ",
    "moduleId": "strategies",
    "title": "Strategy 18: Trendline Break & Retest",
    "summary": "How to draw valid trendlines on gold charts and trade the high-probability break and retest of those trendlines.",
    "body": "# Strategy 18: Trendline Break & Retest\n\n> **The Edge:** A valid trendline represents the rhythm of a trend. When that rhythm breaks and price retests the broken line from the other side, it signals a high-probability shift in direction.\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 The Core Idea\n\nA **trendline** is a diagonal line drawn across a series of swing highs (in a downtrend) or swing lows (in an uptrend). It captures the **pace and angle of a trend**.\n\nWhen a trendline breaks:\n- The trend's rhythm has been disrupted\n- Momentum is shifting\n- A new directional move is likely\n\nThe **retest** of the broken trendline is your entry — the old support becomes resistance, or the old resistance becomes support.\n\n---\n\n## 📐 How to Draw a Valid Trendline\n\n### Uptrend (Support Trendline)\n- Connect **at least two Higher Lows** with a diagonal line sloping upward\n- The more touches the line has, the **stronger** it is\n- Do NOT force the line — it should connect naturally\n\n### Downtrend (Resistance Trendline)\n- Connect **at least two Lower Highs** with a diagonal line sloping downward\n- Again — minimum two touches, preferably three or more\n\n> ✅ **Rule:** A trendline needs a minimum of **2 anchor points** to draw, but only becomes significant with **3 or more touches**. Each touch adds validity.\n\n---\n\n## 📐 Step-by-Step Process (Bearish — Downtrend Trendline Break)\n\n### Step 1 — Draw the Downtrend Trendline (1H or 4H)\n- Connect two or more Lower Highs\n- The line slopes downward from left to right\n- Confirm it has been respected (price has bounced off it)\n\n### Step 2 — Watch for the Break\n- Price pushes through the trendline with a **strong bullish candle**\n- Ideally a **candle body close above** the trendline (not just a wick)\n- The break should look decisive — momentum candle, not a slow grind\n\n### Step 3 — Wait for the Retest\n- After the break, price pulls back down toward the trendline\n- The old resistance trendline is now potential **support**\n- This retest is your entry zone\n\n### Step 4 — Look for a Trigger at the Retest\n- Bullish rejection candle at the trendline (hammer, pin bar, engulfing)\n- Price touches the trendline and immediately bounces\n- 5m bullish break of structure from the retest zone\n\n### Step 5 — Invalidation\n- Stop goes **below the trendline** (for a bullish trade after downtrend break)\n- If price closes back below the trendline, the break was false — exit\n\n### Step 6 — Target\n- First target: Previous swing high (the most recent LH)\n- Second target: Major resistance level beyond\n- Minimum 2R\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Bullish vs Bearish Trendline Break Summary\n\n| | Bullish Break | Bearish Break |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Trendline type** | Downtrend resistance line | Uptrend support line |\n| **Break direction** | Price breaks ABOVE | Price breaks BELOW |\n| **Retest behaviour** | Old resistance → new support | Old support → new resistance |\n| **Trigger** | Bullish rejection at retest | Bearish rejection at retest |\n| **Stop** | Below the trendline | Above the trendline |\n| **Trade** | BUY | SELL |\n\n---\n\n## 🔑 What Makes a Strong Trendline?\n\n| Factor | Why It Matters |\n|---|---|\n| **3+ touches** | More market participants aware of the line |\n| **Consistent angle** | Not too steep (unsustainable) or too flat |\n| **Clean touches** | Price respected the line precisely, not sloppy |\n| **Visible on higher TF** | 4H trendline > 15m trendline in significance |\n| **Long duration** | Weeks-old trendline > hours-old trendline |\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| Drawing trendlines through candle bodies | Always anchor to **wick extremes** |\n| Entering on the break candle itself | Wait for the retest — significantly better R:R |\n| Using trendlines with only 2 touches | Aim for 3+ before trading the break |\n| Forcing lines that don't fit naturally | If you have to force it, it's not a valid trendline |\n| Ignoring HTF context | A trendline break on 5m means little if 4H is strongly trending |\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Pre-Trade Checklist\n\n- [ ] Trendline has at least 3 clear touches\n- [ ] A decisive candle body close beyond the trendline has occurred\n- [ ] Price has pulled back to retest the broken trendline\n- [ ] A trigger candle has confirmed the retest\n- [ ] Stop is placed on the correct side of the trendline\n- [ ] Minimum 2R to the target\n- [ ] HTF context supports the trade direction\n- [ ] No major news event imminent",
